# CVEs with fix versions identified by Trivy but not yet available in the
# AL2023 package repositories.  Remove entries once the fixed packages land.
#
# All entries below verified against a fresh Trivy DB pull (bypassing the
# local --skip-db-update cache ./build normally uses) following the
# 2026-10-28 AL2023 digest refresh (sha256:c04a1012...be9b6). Confirmed via
# `dnf list --showduplicates <pkg>` against the live AL2023 repo mirror that
# no build matching the "Fixed Version" Trivy reports exists yet. All
# previously-listed entries (glib2, libacl, cpython configparser/tarfile/
# unicodedata/BZ2, openssl-fips-provider-latest QUIC DoS) are resolved by
# this digest refresh and have been removed.

# ca-certificates: Firefox website spoofing via failure to block
# compromised intermediate certificates — fix: 2025.2.76-1.0.amzn2023.0.4
# (not yet in repo)
CVE-2026-113470

# curl-minimal / libcurl-minimal: HTTP/2 upload Use-After-Free — fix:
# 8.21.0-5.amzn2023.0.3 (not yet in repo)
CVE-2026-92392

# cyrus-sasl-lib: heap buffer overflow in add_to_challenge() allows
# malicious server to crash client — fix: 2.1.27-18.amzn2023.0.4 (not yet
# in repo)
CVE-2026-107161

# libcap: upstream Go net/http advisories misattributed by Trivy's AL2023
# feed to this package's NVR — fix: 2.73-1.amzn2023.0.8 (not yet in repo)
CVE-2026-78659
CVE-2026-78667
CVE-2026-94440

# pcre2 / pcre2-syntax: out-of-bounds write/read via crafted regular
# expressions and invalid UTF matching — fix: 10.40-1.amzn2023.0.5 (not
# yet in repo)
CVE-2026-103111
CVE-2026-86145
CVE-2026-89156
CVE-2026-89160

# python3 / python3-libs: certificate verification bypass via missing
# server_hostname validation in SSLContext.wrap_bio() — fix:
# 3.9.25-1.amzn2023.0.11 (not yet in repo)
CVE-2026-19553
